  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">West Africa Blue - Community-Centric, High Integrity Blue Carbon Project in Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">West Africa Blue (&#x201c;Blue&#x201d;) is a community-centric, locally-led developer of high integrity, large-scale, blue carbon projects in West Africa. Blue partners with local communities and governments to develop and scale projects that mitigate climate change, protect biodiversity, and enhance community livelihoods, resilience, and adaptation. Blue is offering itself as a market catalyst - sharing learnings, data and models open source, including a fully transparent benefit sharing agreement (BSA). 
Blue&#x2019;s second project in Guinea is modelled on the Sierra Leone project. It builds on engagement with communities in the For&#xe9;cariah and Boffa Prefectures and is led by Blue&#x2019;s local team in Conakry. Supported by a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) and partnership with the Government of Guinea, the project covers a total area of approx. 30,500 ha and includes a mix of mangrove conservation and restoration.</narrative>
  </description>
